course: dictionary
lesson: 5460
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word lantern can mean a lamp you carry, a paper light hung up for a party, or a pumpkin with a face cut in it. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context.
explain: «Now, all in a line, hold the lantern up a bit, Tommy.» Someone is holding it up so people can see, so here a lantern is a lamp you carry. Ask yourself what would fit, then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Candle clocks... kept in a lantern so draughts couldn't make them burn faster.» Here a lantern is a case that keeps the flame safe from the wind. The clue is in the words about draughts and burning.
fact: A lantern is a lamp you can carry, with a light inside a glass or paper case.
fact: A paper lantern is a colourful light hung up for parties and festivals.
fact: A jack-o'-lantern is a pumpkin with a face cut in it and a light inside, made at Halloween.
fact: In history, people carried oil lanterns before electric lights.
fact: Lanterns glow at night in stories and festivals such as Lunar New Year, Diwali and Halloween.
exercise: «Tommy, hold the lantern up a bit so we can see the path.» What is the lantern here? | A pumpkin with a face cut in it | A tall tower on a hill | *A lamp you can carry | A paper light hung up for a party
exercise: Ella hung colourful paper lanterns across the yard for the festival. What is a paper lantern? | *A colourful light hung up for a party or festival | A pumpkin at Halloween | A basket for the shops | A lamp you dig out of the ground
exercise: Mia carved a face into a pumpkin and put a light inside it for Halloween. What is this called? | A camping lamp | A paper lantern | *A jack-o'-lantern | A candle clock
test: «Badger carried a dark lantern, a lantern with a cover to hide the light.» What does the cover on a dark lantern do? | *To hide the light | To make the light brighter | To keep the lantern warm | To hold the handle
test: Which meaning fits best in «The lanterns glowed all night at the Lunar New Year festival»? | Baskets for the shops | Small glass boxes for carrying coins | *Paper lights hung up for a festival | Pumpkins with faces cut in them
exam: Nadia reads «Hold the lantern up» and does not know what lantern means. What should she do first? | Guess and never check | Look it up in a book and stop reading | *Read the words around it and try a meaning that fits | Skip the sentence forever
